# Kernel configuration for the opt-in "amnesia" capability (CAPS=amnesia):
# a read-only root filesystem with targeted tmpfs mounts for the state that
# must still be writable at runtime. No overlayfs, no initrd: the root device
# is mounted ro directly (see lfs's qemu case and package/boot.sh's cmdline
# component, both conditional on "amnesia" in $CAPS), and /var, /tmp, /root
# are separate tmpfs mounts laid down by package/amnesia-config.sh.
#
# There is nothing to turn on here: CONFIG_TMPFS[_POSIX_ACL,_XATTR]=y and
# CONFIG_BTRFS_FS=y already live in base.config (every platform's root is
# btrfs, and tmpfs is needed unconditionally for /run — this capability
# just adds more tmpfs mounts, not tmpfs support itself). This file exists
# anyway, empty of config lines, because linux.sh rejects a capability that
# has no package/linux/<cap>.config.
